findings.body:
The head commit removed the line `jsComponentParametersByIdentifier = jsComponentParameters;` from `enableJSRootComponents`. The base commit had it. The variable is declared at line 14 and is never written anywhere else in the file, so it stays `undefined`.

The only reader is `RootComponentsFunctions.add` at line 30: `jsComponentParametersByIdentifier[componentIdentifier]`. Indexing `undefined` throws a TypeError. That means every `Blazor.rootComponents.add(...)` call fails, including the first-load call in `dynamic-js-root.html`. Restart support is moot if the feature can't add a component at all.

::diff{file="src/Components/Web.JS/src/Rendering/JSRootComponents.ts" lines="120-151"}

::callout{type="warning"}
The removed line sat right above the initializer loop, so it's easy to lose in the restructuring into `if (!hasInitializedJsComponents)`. Restore it unconditionally, outside that block, so the latest circuit's parameter map is always stored.

::suggestion{file="src/Components/Web.JS/src/Rendering/JSRootComponents.ts" lines="136-139"}
currentRendererId = rendererId;
  manager = managerInstance;
  jsComponentParametersByIdentifier = jsComponentParameters;

  if (!hasInitializedJsComponents) {

The guard at line 126 is `if (manager && currentRendererId === rendererId)`. The comment directly under it says a different renderer type should throw, and the PR description says the same: a different `rendererId` (Server 0 vs WASM 1) must throw, and the same `rendererId` on restart must be accepted.

The condition is the opposite of that. Take the two cases:

- **Circuit restart, same renderer ID:** `manager` is set and the IDs match, so the function throws 'Dynamic root components have already been enabled.' That's the bug the PR is supposed to fix.
- **Second host with a different renderer ID:** the IDs differ, so the guard passes and `manager` is silently replaced. The PR says this should throw, and the developer-responsibility note depends on the error being visible.

It's the same unsupported-multi-host situation as before, but now it fails quietly.

::diff{file="src/Components/Web.JS/src/Rendering/JSRootComponents.ts" lines="124-131"}

::callout{type="warning"}
The PR describes two separate semantics, and the guard needs to implement both. Throw only when a manager exists and the renderer differs. Allow a re-enable when the renderer matches. Check which renderer-ID semantics apply across circuits; if IDs are not stable per renderer type, the comparison also needs a different key than `rendererId` alone.

::suggestion{file="src/Components/Web.JS/src/Rendering/JSRootComponents.ts" lines="126-130"}
if (manager && currentRendererId !== rendererId) {
    // A different renderer (e.g., Server vs WebAssembly) is trying to enable JS root components.
    // This is a multi-host scenario which is not supported for dynamic root components.
    throw new Error('Dynamic root components have already been enabled.');
  }

The `--RegisterDynamicJSRootComponent` flag was removed, so `RegisterForJavaScript<ComponentWithPersistentState>("dynamic-js-root-counter")` now runs for every app that uses `RazorComponentEndpointsStartup<App>`. That makes JS root components enabled everywhere that startup is used, not only in the scenario that needs them. Any test using that startup now goes through `attachWebRendererInterop`'s `enableJSRootComponents` path, which changes the baseline for unrelated tests.

The PR description says this reverts the #64159 test architecture, and the removed `Razor Component Endpoints with JS Root Component` site in `Program.cs` is consistent with that. Still, the simpler design is to keep the test-only registration and make the restart test use a dedicated site or flag. Otherwise, reviewers should confirm that the other `RazorComponentEndpointsStartup` tests still pass with JS root components enabled.

::diff{file="src/Components/test/testassets/Components.TestServer/RazorComponentEndpointsStartup.cs" lines="51-55"}
